{"title":"1969 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Show that for any quadrilateral inscribed in a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circle\" title=\"Circle\">circle</a> of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Radius\" title=\"Radius\">radius</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/f/5bf27edd6ee0c25241392922eca9b9c9144f4d73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"17\" /> the length of the shortest side is less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/4/2c4dc1409208ff6a3039f4871d85c16763334983.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"26\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/6/bb60e0857a2c0a2c47acfbe81781032feb1f7150.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c,d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> be the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Edge\" title=\"Edge\">edge</a>-<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Length\" title=\"Length\">lengths</a> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/8/d28c25cf56a155a9784370800f01015be198b4ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e,f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"16\" /> be the lengths of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Diagonal\" title=\"Diagonal\">diagonals</a> of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadrilateral\" title=\"Quadrilateral\">quadrilateral</a>. By <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ptolemy%27s_Theorem\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Ptolemy&#39;s Theorem\">Ptolemy's Theorem</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/e/dfe895d29504f70e64883bd7105acfb49241fa68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab+cd = ef$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"100\" height=\"16\" />. However, each diagonal is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Chord\" title=\"Chord\">chord</a> of the circle and so must be shorter than the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Diameter\" title=\"Diameter\">diameter</a>: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/0/150d4a976356965231320e49cad499192e37f391.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e,f \\le 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" /> and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/c/aacfdbf5ba649dcc918fdd64e88292b99029c355.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab+cd \\le 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"92\" height=\"17\" />. \n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/3/023edac02df464f2a83d0b9b79f02a850835e86c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c,d &gt; \\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"108\" height=\"20\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/2/ab2d17c614c6bb6e42e0ce2e6669d88b349e4307.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab+cd &gt; 4,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" /> which is impossible. Thus, at least one of the sides must have length less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/b/75bec5f95356b5621c8c473003558d5d8187a4d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that the shortest side would subtend the smallest angle at the center of the circle. It is easily provable that this angle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7dfa8a2a90d521b2b03f5b82a1fb9f85dce88c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />, because had all 4 angles been greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7dfa8a2a90d521b2b03f5b82a1fb9f85dce88c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />, the sum of the subtended angles would have been greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/b/96bd59024f5cb49b070ca9b0f8906499940c75e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$360^{\\circ}$\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" />, which is impossible as the sum should be exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/b/96bd59024f5cb49b070ca9b0f8906499940c75e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$360^{\\circ}$\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" />. Hence, atleast one (but not all 4) of the angles would be less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7dfa8a2a90d521b2b03f5b82a1fb9f85dce88c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" /> and so the smallest one most certainly is also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/7/8072de36d39df5ee4fdd6b41e1d4d583d7fecc5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\leq 90^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />. \n</p><p>Now assuming the angle between the two radii at the ends of the smallest side is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the length of the smallest side is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/a/58aec9783ead7e4ae247e76cc334067c7576e8fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2 - 2 cos \\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"92\" height=\"21\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/d/72d478108f2eabbb9c9d4be00147a225d207b4ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$cos \\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"36\" height=\"14\" /> is positive in the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/b/a3b5296de67b137847f7fc7860f15c1ba5fc9331.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0, 90^{\\circ})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"59\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/2/7225a684b65ad17033d6b212fe609a14e790e1f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2- 2 cos \\theta \\leq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"110\" height=\"17\" /> and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/2/0327a112a58fe9bb5214266bef8b6321b0070b14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2 - 2 cos \\theta } \\leq \\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"140\" height=\"22\" />. \n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_Canadian_MO\" title=\"1969 Canadian MO\">1969 Canadian MO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_Canadian_MO_Problems\" title=\"1969 Canadian MO Problems\">Problems</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1969 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1969 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1969 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1969 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1969 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1969 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1969 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1969 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1969 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1969 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 10\">10</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1969 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><br />\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016193605\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.030 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.044 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 134/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1023/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 62/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3876/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    8.974      1 Template:Old_CanadaMO_box\n100.00%    8.974      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3618:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261016193605 and revision id 288437. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}